\begin{align*}
-g_1 + 3g_1 (1 - r) + g_1 r^3 &= 0 \\
-g_1 + 3g_1 - 3g_1 r + g_1 r^3 &= 0 \\
g_1 (r^3 - 3r + 2) &= 0
\end{align*}
Since \(g_1 \neq 0\), we have:
\begin{align*}
r^3 - 3r + 2 &= 0 \\
(r - 1)(r^2 + r - 2) &= 0 \\
(r - 1)(r - 1)(r + 2) &= 0 \\
(r - 1)^2 (r + 2) &= 0
\end{align*}
Thus, \(r = 1\) or \(r = -2\). If \(r = 1\), then from Equation 2, \(g_1 (1 - 1)^2 = 1\), which is a contradiction. Therefore, \(r = -2\).

Substituting \(r = -2\) into Equation 2:
\begin{align*}
